[center][size=6][b]Event-PVP-Plugin 1.0.9 — Compact Changelog[/b][/size][/center]

A concise overview of all new features, improvements, fixes, and breaking changes in version [b]1.0.9[/b].

[hr]

[size=5][b]Key Highlights & New Features[/b][/size]

[size=4][color=#57bb57][b]1. Integrated Inventory Management ([font=courier new]InventoryBackup[/font])[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Built-in Inventory Safety[/b]: Replaced legacy snapshot files with [font=courier new]InventoryBackup[/font] ([url=https://modrinth.com/project/rpKY25cW]Modrinth[/url]) as a mandatory dependency ([font=courier new]depend:[/font] in [font=courier new]plugin.yml[/font]).
[*][b]Automatic Restore Net[/b]: Inventories are backed up before arena/lobby teleports and restored on match/event end, respawn, or rejoin.
[*][b]Crash Protection[/b]: Active sessions are written to [font=courier new]inventory-guard.yml[/font] and restored automatically on server restart.
[*][b]Legacy Mode[/b]: Set [font=courier new]settings.inventory-management.provider: "none"[/font] if you prefer Multiverse-Inventories.
[/list]

[size=4][color=#57bb57][b]2. Player Location Safety & Anti-Strand System[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Return Location Journal ([font=courier new]player-return-locations.yml[/font])[/b]: Player return coordinates are saved synchronously before any teleport.
[*][b]Automatic Self-Rescue[/b]: Players stranded in an event or arena world after a server crash/disconnect are returned to their origin upon reconnecting.
[*][b]Unified [font=courier new]SafeLocationResolver[/font][/b]: Prevents players from spawning in the void or becoming trapped in unloaded worlds.
[*][b]New Command [font=courier new]/eventpvp rescue[/font][/b]: Admins can inspect ([font=courier new]list[/font]), rescue stranded players ([font=courier new]<player>[/font]), or clean stale sessions ([font=courier new]clean[/font]).
[*][b]Persistent Payout Queue ([font=courier new]pending-payouts.yml[/font])[/b]: Queues wager winnings and event rewards for players who disconnect before payout.
[/list]

[size=4][color=#57bb57][b]3. Complete Web Interface Overhaul[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Dedicated 3-Tab Inventory Manager[/b] (Explorer / Sessions / Settings): Search backups, inspect inventories via authentic Minecraft Canvas with XP bar, restore after a confirmation prompt, and monitor live sessions. Restores are capped at 10 per minute and refused while the player has an open guard session.
[*][b]Multiverse World Management[/b]: Create, import, load, unload, delete (with safety checks), and backup/restore worlds directly in the web panel. Works with both Multiverse-Core 4 (command backend) and 5 (API backend).
[*][b]Server Resource Pack Textures[/b]: Optionally extracts and displays custom item textures from the server's resource pack ([font=courier new]items.resource-pack.enabled[/font], off by default, size-capped). Only direct replacements under [font=courier new]assets/minecraft/textures/item/[/font] are used — CustomModelData is deliberately not evaluated.
[*][b]Dynamic Material Catalog[/b]: Loads valid materials and enchantment limits directly from the server ([font=courier new]GET /api/materials[/font]).
[*][b]Deep-Snapshot Precision Dirty Tracking[/b]: Baseline comparison ([font=courier new]CONFIG_BASELINE[/font] & [font=courier new]isDeepEqual[/font]) eliminates false-positive "Unsaved Changes" badges when reverting edits or saving unmodified modals.
[*][b]Web Server Settings[/b]:
  [list]
  [*]Configurable [b]Public URL[/b] with automatic [font=courier new]{port}[/font] substitution for [font=courier new]/eventpvp webtoken[/font].
  [*][b]Port Change Safety Warning[/b]: Confirmation dialog before saving port changes to prevent accidental disconnection.
  [*]New [b][font=courier new]web.bind-address[/font][/b]: empty for all interfaces, [font=courier new]"127.0.0.1"[/font] when a reverse proxy (Nginx, Caddy, Cloudflare Tunnel) sits in front.
  [*]Removed [font=courier new]items.local-texture-path[/font] and [font=courier new]items.block-texture-source[/font] in favor of [font=courier new]items.resource-pack.*[/font].
  [/list]
[/list]

[size=4][color=#57bb57][b]4. 100% Localization & Zero Hardcoded Messages[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]7 Supported Languages[/b]: English, German, Spanish, French, Japanese, Polish, Russian with 100% key parity (1097 keys per [font=courier new]messages_*.yml[/font], 764 keys per [font=courier new]web/lang/*.json[/font]).
[*][b]Console & Logger Localization[/b]: All logger, startup, shutdown, and error messages are fully translated via [font=courier new]messages.console.*[/font].
[*][b]Embedded Fallback System[/b]: Incomplete translation files fall back to embedded English defaults instead of failing or printing raw keys.
[*][b]Automated Audit Suite ([font=courier new]tools/i18n_audit.py[/font])[/b]: 0 findings across all 11 detection rules (D1–D11).
[/list]

[size=4][color=#57bb57][b]5. Streamlined Configuration & Debug Mode[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Persistent Debug Switch[/b]: [font=courier new]/eventpvp debug (on | on full | off | status)[/font] saved to [font=courier new]settings.debug[/font] in [font=courier new]config.yml[/font].
[*][b]Decoupled World Management[/b]: Replaced ambiguous [font=courier new]world-loading[/font] with two independent booleans: [font=courier new]settings.world-management.events[/font] and [font=courier new]settings.world-management.arenas[/font].
[*][b]Switchable Lobby Phase ([font=courier new]use-lobby[/font])[/b]: Events can run with or without a separate lobby phase.
[*][b]Automatic Config Migration[/b]: Existing configs are automatically updated on first startup without losing custom values or comments.
[/list]

[hr]

[size=5][color=#e8a838][b]Breaking Changes & Upgrades[/b][/color][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Required Dependencies:[/b] [url=https://modrinth.com/project/3wmN97b8]Multiverse-Core[/url] (v4/v5), [url=https://modrinth.com/project/ayRaM8J7]VaultUnlocked[/url] (or classic [url=https://www.spigotmc.org/resources/vault.34315/]Vault[/url]), and [url=https://modrinth.com/project/rpKY25cW]InventoryBackup[/url] are now mandatory in [font=courier new]plugin.yml[/font].
[*][b]Removed Command:[/b] [font=courier new]/inventoryrestore[/font] is removed. Use [font=courier new]/inv <player>[/font] or the Web Panel instead.
[*][b]Removed Permissions:[/b] [font=courier new]eventpvp.inventory.restore[/font] and [font=courier new]eventpvp.inventory.restore.any[/font] are removed.
[*][b]World Loading Config:[/b] [font=courier new]settings.world-loading[/font] is migrated to [font=courier new]settings.world-management.events[/font] and [font=courier new].arenas[/font].
[*][b]Inventory Config:[/b] [font=courier new]settings.inventory-snapshots.*[/font] is migrated to [font=courier new]settings.inventory-management.*[/font]. [font=courier new]retain-days[/font], [font=courier new]default-group[/font], [font=courier new]groups[/font], and [font=courier new]ids.*[/font] are dropped — retention is now InventoryBackup's job.
[*][b]Legacy Snapshot Files:[/b] [font=courier new]inventory_backups.yml[/font] and [font=courier new]inventory_post_backups.yml[/font] are no longer read. They stay on disk untouched.
[*][b]Equipment Merge:[/b] [font=courier new]equipment:[/font], [font=courier new]equipment-sets:[/font], and [font=courier new]equipment-groups:[/font] are merged into a single [font=courier new]equipment:[/font]. On an ID collision the [font=courier new]equipment:[/font] entry wins; the other is kept as [font=courier new]<id>-legacy[/font] and logged.
[*][b]Web Config:[/b] [font=courier new]items.local-texture-path[/font] and [font=courier new]items.block-texture-source[/font] are replaced by [font=courier new]items.resource-pack.*[/font].
[*][b]Command Restrictions:[/b] [font=courier new]settings.command-restriction[/font] values [font=courier new]join[/font] and [font=courier new]pvp[/font] become [font=courier new]both[/font].
[/list]

[hr]

[size=5][b]Command & Permission Quick Reference[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]New & Updated Commands[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][font=courier new]/eventpvp rescue <list|player|clean>[/font] [b](new)[/b]
Permission: [font=courier new]eventpvp.admin[/font]
Description: Inspect, rescue, and clean stranded player sessions

[*][font=courier new]/eventpvp debug <on|on full|off|status>[/font] [b](updated)[/b]
Permission: [font=courier new]eventpvp.debug[/font]
Description: Toggle and inspect debug logging — the level is now persisted in [font=courier new]settings.debug[/font]

[*][font=courier new]/eventpvp webtoken[/font] [b](unchanged)[/b]
Permission: [font=courier new]eventpvp.admin.web[/font] (or [font=courier new]eventpvp.admin[/font])
Description: Generate a secure one-time login token for the Web Panel

[*][font=courier new]/eventpvp reload[/font] [b](unchanged)[/b]
Permission: [font=courier new]eventpvp.admin[/font]
Description: Reload all configurations and language bundles

[*][font=courier new]/eventpvp version[/font] [b](unchanged)[/b]
Permission: [font=courier new]eventpvp.admin[/font]
Description: Check plugin version and update status

[*][font=courier new]/inv <player>[/font] [b](external)[/b]
Permission: [font=courier new]inventoryrestore.admin[/font]
Description: Inspect and restore inventory backups — provided by the InventoryBackup plugin, not by Event-PVP-Plugin
[/list]

[size=4][b]New Permissions[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][font=courier new]pvpwager.spectate.all[/font]: Spectate matches that already reached the spectator limit (default: [font=courier new]op[/font]).
[*][font=courier new]pvpwager.nowager[/font]: Start a match without any wager (default: [font=courier new]op[/font]).
[/list]

[font=courier new]eventpvp.admin.web[/font], [font=courier new]eventpvp.debug[/font], and [font=courier new]eventpvp.debug.receive[/font] already existed in 1.0.8 and are unchanged.

[size=4][b]Removed Permissions[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][font=courier new]eventpvp.inventory.restore[/font] and [font=courier new]eventpvp.inventory.restore.any[/font] — remove them from your permission plugin.
[/list]
